british-english: the word list Quill checks spelling with, one word a line (UTF-8).

It is SCOWL's British English list (size 50, from Debian's wbritish 2020.12.07) without the
possessive forms ("'s"; Quill accepts those for any word), with a few dozen words added that
documents about computers often use (footer, endnote, email, website...). SCOWL is
Copyright 2000-2011 Kevin Atkinson and others; see LICENSE-dict.txt for its terms.

Words added with "Add to Dictionary" go to Quill.words next to Quill, not here.

th_en.dat: the English thesaurus (Review > Thesaurus, Synonyms on the right-button menu), in MyThes's
format. It is made by tools/mkthes.py from LibreOffice's th_en_US_v2 (made from Princeton's WordNet):
the words in british-english, up to four meanings of six synonyms each. WordNet's licence is in
LICENSE-thesaurus.txt.

hyph_de_DE.dic, hyph_fr_FR.dic, hyph_es_ES.dic, hyph_it_IT.dic, hyph_pt_PT.dic, hyph_nl_NL.dic,
hyph_pl_PL.dic: hyphenation patterns for text in those languages, made by tools/mkhyph.py from the
hyph-utf8 patterns (see each .txt and LICENSE-hyph.txt).

Other languages: put a Hunspell dictionary here, named by its language (de_DE.aff and de_DE.dic, or
de.aff and de.dic), and Quill checks text in that language with it; th_de_DE.dat (a MyThes thesaurus)
and hyph_de_DE.dic (Hyphen patterns) work the same way.
